messages:
marcus.s: FYI — Acme hitting 404s using TS SDK when calling responses.create for chat. They see `Error: 404 route not found`.

acme-sre: Repro steps:
1) npm install @redwood/inference@0.8.1
2) run index.ts (snippet below)

acme-sre: ```ts
import Redwood from '@redwood/inference';
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });
await client.responses.create({ model: 'redwood-1', input: 'hello' });
```

jordan.eng: That matches a known break — we renamed the route in 0.9.0 from `responses.create` -> `chat.generate` and also changed `model` -> `modelName`.

marcus.s: They can't upgrade easily (locked build). Any temporary workaround?

priya.devex: Quick options: 1) call the REST endpoint directly with `fetch`/curl; 2) install a tiny wrapper that maps old call to new shape; 3) we can push a compatibility shim server-side for a short window.

priya.devex: Example direct call:
```
curl -X POST https://api.redwood.ai/v1/chat.generate \n  -H "Authorization: Bearer $RW_KEY" \n  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \n  -d '{\"modelName\":\"redwood-1\",\"input\":\"hello\"}'
```

jordan.eng: I've created INF-2345 and a small hotfix that adds 404 hints. Also scheduling a short-lived shim that accepts `responses.create` and translates `model` -> `modelName` at the gateway.

marcus.s: Please add the exact package version we should tell Acme to upgrade to.

priya.devex: Tell them to upgrade to `@redwood/inference@0.9.2` (contains route rename docs and typings). Command: `npm i @redwood/inference@^0.9.2`.

acme-sre: Can you share the minimal transpile-free JS snippet we can drop in their runtime to avoid full upgrade?

priya.devex: Sure — tiny shim:
```js
// shim.js
const Old = require('@redwood/inference');
module.exports = function oldClient(opts){
  const c = new Old({ ...opts });
  const oldCreate = c.responses?.create;
  c.responses = c.responses || {};
  c.responses.create = async (params) => {
    const newParams = { modelName: params.model, input: params.input };
    return c.chat.generate(newParams);
  };
  return c;
};
```

jordan.eng: Note: this is temporary; recommend they schedule upgrade. We'll also emit a breaking-change note in changelog and alert ops about the shim.

deploy-bot: deploy prod-gateway-shim v0.1 -> staging

marcus.s: Thanks all — I'll pass the shim and upgrade instruction to Acme, and flag for the account team. :thumbsup:
